# Anything env-shaped. The bare `.env` rule that used to be here matched only
# that exact name, so live-secret files like `.env.bak.1786883074` and
# `.env.pre-monad-backup` sat untracked-but-committable — one `git add -A` from
# publishing an OpenAI key and the production Postgres/Redis credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
